.TH tkutree n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkutree
.PP
A thin \fBttk::treeview\fR wrapper for hierarchical data: build a tree (optional data columns and a scrollbar), insert nodes, load a nested structure in one call, and read selection / text / values back.
.SS API
.CS
set w [::tkutils::tkutree::widget .tr ?-columns ids? ?-headings texts? \
        ?-show spec? ?-height n? ?-command cmd?]
::tkutils::tkutree::insert    $w parent text ?-values list? ?-open bool? ?-id id?
::tkutils::tkutree::loadTree  $w nodes
::tkutils::tkutree::selection $w
::tkutils::tkutree::itemText  $w id
::tkutils::tkutree::children  $w ?id?
::tkutils::tkutree::treeview  $w        ;# the underlying ttk::treeview
.CE
.PP
\fBloadTree\fR takes a list of node dicts; keys per node: \fBtext\fR (required), \fBvalues\fR, \fBopen\fR, \fBid\fR, \fBchildren\fR (a list of nodes). \fB\-command\fR is called with the selection list on \fB<<TreeviewSelect>>\fR.
